meta {
  name: Cancel Production
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurant_id}}/production/orders/{{production_order_id}}/cancel
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
      "wasted_qty": 5,
      "waste_reason": "other"
  }
}

docs {
  Owner/manager/chef. Takes a requested or cooking production off the board. The body is optional.

  wasted_qty (optional, in the dish's prepared unit): what a started batch already used before it was called off. Its recipe leaves raw stock as waste (never blocks — stock may go negative), it is logged in the waste register (source prepared_dish, production_order_id set), and the order keeps wasted_qty.
  waste_reason: cooking_error (default) | damaged | other

  422 on wasted_qty when the production is still requested ("The kitchen had not started this production, so nothing was used.").
  422 on order when it is already completed or cancelled.
}
